  "officialHtml": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-a100.html",
  "prefLabel": "Env-A 105.31 Type 0 waste",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-A 105.31 “Type 0 waste” means a mixture of highly combustible waste from commercial and industrial activities, including but not limited to paper, cardboard, wood, and combustible floor sweepings, that has a heating value of at least 4718 calories per gram, equivalent to 8500 BTUs per pound, as fired, and contains:\n\n(a) Up to 10 percent by weight of plastic bags, coated paper, laminated paper, treated corrugated cardboard, oily rags, and plastic or rubber scraps;\n\n(b) Up to 10 percent moisture; and\n\n(c) Up to 5 percent incombustible solids by weight.\n\nSource. #7845, eff 3-8-03 (formerly Env-A 101.293(a)); renumbered by #8256 (from Env-A 101.283), (see Revision Note #1 at chapter heading); renumbered by #8304 (see Revision Note #2 at chapter heading); renumbered by #9839 (from Env-A 101.197), (see Revision Note #3 at chapter heading); ss by #13105, eff 9-25-20 (formerly Env-A 101.199) (see Revision Note #4 at chapter heading for Env-A 100)",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-a100.html"
